# Auto-commit after completed work

When the user asks you to do something and you finish the implementation (code, build, docs, or other project changes):

1. **Always create a git commit** for those changes in the same turn, without waiting to be asked again.
2. Follow the existing git commit protocol (status, diff, log, stage relevant files, HEREDOC message, verify status).
3. Do **not** push unless the user also asks to push (or says “commit and push”).
4. Skip commit only if there are genuinely no changes, or the user explicitly said not to commit.
5. Prefer concise commit messages focused on why; bump version when the project already versions releases.
